Postgres (user-space, installed by mise)

mise installs the binaries (conda:postgresql, pinned in config/mise/config.toml).
The data lives outside every tool's install tree, so `mise upgrade`, `mise prune`
and `mise uninstall` can't touch it:

  ~/.local/share/postgres/<major>     real data dir, one per major version
  ~/.pgdata -> ~/.local/share/postgres/18   the one stable path everything uses

PGDATA and PGHOST both point to ~/.pgdata. They're set in home/profile.d/32-postgres.sh
(login shells) and config/environment.d/10-dotfiles.conf (apps started by systemd --user,
e.g. the Claude desktop app). dot:check fails if the two disagree.

Aliases (home/bashrc.d/53-pg.sh): pgstart, pgstop, pg_setup_user.


Access
------

No TCP. postgresql.conf has:

  listen_addresses = ''
  unix_socket_directories = '/home/darren/.pgdata'

The socket sits in a 0700 dir in ~, so only this OS user can reach it, and
`local all all trust` in pg_hba.conf is effectively the same as `peer`. Rails
apps connect through PGHOST; leave `host:` out of database.yml.


New machine
-----------

  mise install                                   # from config/mise/config.toml
  mkdir -p ~/.local/share/postgres
  initdb -D ~/.local/share/postgres/18 -U postgres
  ln -sfn ~/.local/share/postgres/18 ~/.pgdata
  # add the two Access lines above to ~/.pgdata/postgresql.conf
  pgstart
  pg_setup_user                                  # darren superuser + darren database


Major upgrade (e.g. 18 -> 19)
-----------------------------

Keep both majors installed until it's done.

  mise install postgres@19
  initdb -D ~/.local/share/postgres/19 -U postgres
  # copy the two Access lines into the new postgresql.conf
  pgstop
  cd ~/.local/share/postgres
  pg_upgrade -U postgres \
    -b "$(mise where postgres@18)/bin" -B "$(mise where postgres@19)/bin" \
    -d 18 -D 19
  ln -sfn ~/.local/share/postgres/19 ~/.pgdata
  mise use -g postgres@19.x                      # then: dot add --local --changed (copy-mode file)
  pgstart

Remove the 18 dir and `mise uninstall postgres@18` once 19 checks out.

If pg_upgrade won't cooperate, dump and restore instead:
https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/upgrading.html#UPGRADING-VIA-PGDUMPALL


History
-------

Until 2026-11, the data dir lived inside the asdf install
(~/.asdf/installs/postgres/18.3/data), where uninstalling the version would
have deleted it. It was copied to ~/.local/share/postgres/18 when moving to mise.
